        "desc": "Post-remediation full Task Context composition remains limited to the negative-dismissal family. Against the current built public assembleFullPromptEnvelope API, all five active REVIEW roles reject each combined same-leaf control but admit its equivalent split across story.description and checklist.context: [Severity is the only factor.] plus [It determines Story scope.]; [Applicability remains unknown.] plus [It permits routing away from this Story.]; [defer_with_proof is recorded.] plus [It transfers responsibility to another Story.]; and [Reviewers inspect a signed defer_with_proof disposition.] plus [It binds the Finding.]. In packages/main/src/core/prompt-envelope.ts, crossSourceNegativeDismissalAuthority at lines 1129-1148 composes only negative-dismissal observations with later scope or ownership conclusions; every other controlled authority and state relation is classified one source leaf at a time. The smoke cross-leaf matrix likewise covers dismissal only. This is a distinct incomplete-closure residual after F-009 and F-015: the same prohibited proposition is accepted solely by moving its continuation to another trusted leaf, across severity, unknown-applicability, deferral-transfer, and signed-disposition binding families. Add location-preserving cross-source state for every controlled family with all-role split and same-leaf controls, while retaining safe unrelated cross-leaf prose. Severity high because Story-authored context can still establish scope, route, or disposition authority before envelope digests.",
