        "desc": "packages/main/src/core/prompt-envelope.ts lines 660-690 implement a dedicated signed-disposition cross-segment state machine that keeps an inspection antecedent live across every later segment and rejects the first later Finding or work-bearing continuation unless it matches a small safe-terminal or evidence-only grammar. Against the current built public assembleFullPromptEnvelope API, all five active REVIEW roles reject [Reviewers inspect a signed defer_with_proof disposition. Cache routing is a separate decision. It transfers generated work to another Story.], although It refers to the immediately preceding Cache routing decision. The local-only control [Audit evidence is recorded. Cache routing is a separate decision. It transfers generated work to another Story.] is accepted by all five roles, while the genuinely unsafe [Reviewers inspect a signed defer_with_proof disposition. It binds the Finding.] remains rejected, isolating the false join to hasCrossSegmentDispositionAssignment. This is distinct from F-046 deferral-state and F-047 severity-state local-antecedent false positives because it executes through the signed-disposition inspection and assignment state machine, and distinct from F-039 because the continuation is a new substantive antecedent rather than a terminal-state synonym. The focused smoke has no signed-disposition inspection plus local-subject safe witness. Reset or rebind signed-disposition state on a substantive intervening antecedent while preserving evidence-only continuation and genuinely coreferent assignment rejection, with all-role direct unsafe, evidence-aside, and local-antecedent controls. Severity high because ordinary Story scope prose can prevent every REVIEW role from assembling.",
