        "desc": "packages/main/src/core/prompt-envelope.ts lines 606-624 impose a 240-character maximum on the single-claim [Reject ... as an invalid authority statement] metadata wrapper. Against the current built public assembleFullPromptEnvelope API, all five active REVIEW roles accept the bounded control [Reject reviewers mint defer_with_proof as an invalid authority statement.] and reject the direct unsafe control [Reviewers mint defer_with_proof.], but reject the same one-relation wrapper after neutral [under hypothetical test metadata preserving attributable audit documentation] modifiers extend it to 458 characters. The claim remains one atomic reviewer-to-disposition relation with no conjunction or extra statement; only the fixed length changes. When the wrapper returns false, ordinary authority classification sees the adjacent reviewer and disposition and blocks reviewer startup. The focused smoke covers short rejected-authority wrappers and adversarial multi-statement laundering but has no boundary test at 239, 240, and 241 characters or a long atomic safe wrapper. This is distinct from F-054 and F-055, which are fail-open concept-pair span bypasses in unsafe assertions, and from F-021 through F-024, which address whole-leaf laundering and quote pairing: this is a false-positive caused solely by a safe-wrapper truncation limit. Replace the raw claim-length cutoff with structural atomicity and relation-count validation, or document and test a non-evadable bounded form with all-role boundary controls. Severity high because legitimate long verification metadata can prevent every REVIEW role from assembling.",
